meta {
  name: Drop the elective
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subject-enrollments/{{electiveEnrollmentId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "dropped",
    "dropped_on": "2026-10-01"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq dropped
  res.body.subject_offering_id: eq {{electiveOfferingId}}
}

docs {
  A pupil who gives up French is dropped, not deleted. The row stays, with the
  date it ended, because a term of French that was actually taught has to
  survive on the record it was reported on.

  Which is why the listing at 08/04 still counts this pupil against the French
  offering afterwards: the default listing is not filtered by status. Ask for
  status=active when the question is who is sitting the subject now.

  There is no GET /subject-enrollments/{id}: a single subject enrolment is
  only ever read as part of a pupil's set, which 05/07 lists.
}
